# zh-CN translations adopted with the five English source cards.

@event stables_hippogriff_grooming
# en: Feathers the Wrong Way
title [08770c] = 逆着长的羽毛
# en: {A hippogriff has rolled in the mud and lies in her stall with every feather pointing the wrong way, waiting to be groomed.|The muddy hippogriff again. She lies down the moment she sees you with a brush.|The hippogriff has kept her muddiest wing for you, and holds it out like a gift.} {season == "autumn": Leaves are stuck in her feathers.|{The stable cat supervises from a beam.|The owls are watching to see if you get it wrong.|Brask is somewhere nearby, humming to a feed sack.}}
text [cd2c78] = {一头鹰头马身有翼兽在泥里打了个滚，躺在厩栏里，每根羽毛都朝着反方向，等人来梳理。|又是那头满身泥的鹰头马身有翼兽。她一看见你拿着刷子就躺下了。|鹰头马身有翼兽把最脏的那只翅膀留给了你，像献礼一样伸过来。} {season == "autumn": 她的羽毛里卡着落叶。|{马厩的猫在横梁上监工。|猫头鹰们等着看你出错。|布拉斯克就在附近，对着一袋饲料哼歌。}}
# en: A student brushing the wing feathers of a lying-down hippogriff in a straw-filled stall, loose feathers drifting in a shaft of light.
scene [302c3b] = 铺满稻草的厩栏里，一名学生在给一头卧着的鹰头马身有翼兽梳理翅羽，散落的羽毛在一束光里飘浮。
# en: Groom her properly, feather by feather
opt.left.label [eded20] = 一根一根，好好梳
# en: {It takes the whole afternoon and both your arms. She falls asleep with her head on your boot, which is the highest mark a hippogriff gives.|You do it the slow way, with the grain. She clicks her beak at you every time you're right, and once, gently, when you're wrong.|You know her feathers now. She lets you do the hard bit under the wing, and Brask, passing, says nothing at all.}
opt.left.say.1 [9888b4] = {这花了整整一个下午，外加你的两条胳膊。她把头搁在你的靴子上睡着了，这是鹰头马身有翼兽能给的最高评价。|你慢慢来，顺着羽毛的走向梳。每次梳对，她就冲你咔哒一下喙；梳错时也咔哒一下，很轻。|你现在熟悉她的羽毛了。她让你梳翅膀底下最难的那块。布拉斯克路过，一个字也没说。}
# en: Read Brask's grooming notes on the wall
opt.right.label [2c0b1f] = 读墙上布拉斯克的梳理笔记
# en: {The notes are long, opinionated and illustrated. You learn a great deal about feathers. The hippogriff stays muddy and sighs at you.|You read the notes. Brask catches you at it and says, "She doesn't need a scholar, she needs a brush."|You finish the notes, which you could recite by now, and leave the brush for someone else. The hippogriff looks away.}
opt.right.say.1 [49fcee] = {笔记又长又固执，还配了插图。你学到了很多关于羽毛的知识。鹰头马身有翼兽依旧满身泥，冲你叹了口气。|你读着笔记。布拉斯克撞见了，说：“她不需要学者，她需要一把刷子。”|你把笔记读完了，现在都能背下来了，然后把刷子留给了别人。鹰头马身有翼兽扭开了头。}

@event stables_tack_room
# en: The Tack Room
title [a30d64] = 马具间
# en: {The tack room is a mess of harnesses, and the oil pot is out. Someone has to do the straps before Beastcraft tomorrow.|The tack room again. The griffon chick has been at the buckles.|The tack room has your bucket in it now, the one you sit on.} {season == "winter": It's the warmest room in the stables, and it smells of leather and oil.|{One strap has teeth marks all along it.|A saddle is missing; nobody wants to say whose.|There is a nest in the old harness, and it is occupied.}}
text [036030] = {马具间里的挽具乱成一团，油罐已经摆出来了。明天驭兽课之前，总得有人把皮带收拾好。|又是马具间。狮鹫幼崽把扣环啃过了。|马具间里现在有你的桶了，就是你坐的那只。} {season == "winter": 这是马厩里最暖和的屋子，满是皮革和油的味道。|{有一根皮带上从头到尾都是牙印。|少了一副马鞍，谁也不肯说是谁的。|旧挽具里有个窝，而且有主了。}}
# en: A cramped tack room hung with harnesses and saddles, a student sitting on an upturned bucket oiling a strap, a griffon chick peering in at the door.
scene [fded30] = 挂满挽具和马鞍的狭小马具间，一名学生坐在倒扣的桶上给皮带上油，一只狮鹫幼崽从门口探进头来。
# en: Oil and mend the straps
opt.left.label [692558] = 给皮带上油、修补
# en: {You oil straps until your hands are black and the room smells like a cobbler's. Every buckle works. Nobody thanks you, which is how you know it's done.|You mend the bitten strap and replace the buckle the chick swallowed. It will reappear, Brask says darkly.|You do the straps by touch now, talking to the nest in the old harness. Its owner answers.}
opt.left.say.1 [970da8] = {你给皮带上油，直到双手乌黑，屋里闻起来像鞋匠铺。每个扣环都好使了。没人道谢，你就知道活干完了。|你补好了被咬的皮带，换掉了幼崽吞下去的扣环。布拉斯克阴沉地说，它会再冒出来的。|你现在闭着眼都能收拾皮带，一边干一边跟旧挽具里的窝说话。窝的主人回了话。}
# en: Slip out before anyone hands you the pot
opt.right.label [120ded] = 趁没人递油罐，溜走
# en: {You leave the straps for the morning. In the morning Brask hands you the pot, and a look.|You're out of the door before the oil pot is. Behind you the griffon chick starts on another buckle.|You slip away. You hear Brask say your name to the hippogriffs, in a tone.}
opt.right.say.1 [9ce37f] = {你把皮带留到早上。到了早上，布拉斯克把油罐递给你，外加一个眼神。|油罐还没递过来，你已经出门了。身后，狮鹫幼崽开始啃另一个扣环。|你溜走了。你听见布拉斯克对着鹰头马身有翼兽们念你的名字，语气不太妙。}

@event courtyard_fountain_wishes
# en: Coins in the Fountain
title [fa2295] = 喷泉里的硬币
# en: {Students throw coins in the courtyard fountain for luck before exams. The coins are still there, glinting.|The fountain is full of exam-luck again.|You know exactly how many coins are in the fountain this week, and that is a bad sign.} {season == "winter": The water is cold enough to make your teeth ache by looking at it.|{A sign says the coins go to the infirmary fund.|A first-year is throwing in a coin with a long, whispered wish.|The fountain is freezing at one edge, as it does when it shouldn't.}}
text [30a6f7] = {学生们考试前会往庭院喷泉里扔硬币求好运。硬币还在水底闪着光。|喷泉里又满是考试的好运了。|你清楚地知道这周喷泉里有多少枚硬币，这可不是好兆头。} {season == "winter": 那水冷得光是看着都牙疼。|{一块牌子写着硬币归医务室基金。|一个一年级生扔进一枚硬币，许了个又长又小声的愿。|喷泉的一边结冰了，就像它不该结冰时那样。}}
# en: A courtyard fountain with coins glinting on the bottom, a student crouching at the rim with a sleeve rolled up, a groundskeeper's rake leaning nearby.
scene [281e8f] = 庭院喷泉的水底闪着硬币，一名学生卷起袖子蹲在池边，旁边靠着一把园丁的耙子。
# en: Fish out a few coins for yourself
opt.left.label [dbe634] = 给自己捞几枚
# en: {Nobody's watching. Your sleeve is soaked to the shoulder and your pocket is heavier. The sign about the infirmary fund keeps looking at you.|You fish quickly and walk away fast. A first-year's wish is in your pocket now, and the coin is warm.|You've become good at this, which is not a compliment.}
opt.left.say.1 [618a0c] = {没人看着。你的袖子湿到了肩膀，口袋沉了一些。那块医务室基金的牌子一直盯着你。|你捞得飞快，走得更快。一个一年级生的愿望现在在你口袋里，那枚硬币还是温的。|你已经很擅长这个了，这可不是夸奖。}
# en: Throw one in yourself
opt.right.label [b7ed27] = 自己也扔一枚
# en: {You throw a coin and wish for something you won't admit to. It's the best you've felt all week.|You throw your coin in after the first-year's. They grin at you, as if you're in on something together.|You throw a coin in. It lands on top of an old one of yours, which you take to mean something.}
opt.right.say.1 [5b0af7] = {你扔了一枚硬币，许了个你不会承认的愿。这是你这一周最好的时刻。|你跟着那个一年级生扔了一枚。{they}冲你咧嘴一笑，好像你们一起知道了什么秘密。|你扔了一枚硬币。它落在你以前扔的一枚上面，你觉得这总有点意思。}

@event courtyard_lost_cat
# en: Footnote on the Wall
title [bc5a1f] = 墙头上的脚注
# en: {Footnote, the library cat, is sitting on top of the courtyard wall and refusing to come down. A small crowd has gathered.|Footnote is on the courtyard wall again, being worshipped.|Footnote is on the wall. The crowd parts for you, as the expert.} {season == "spring": Blossom is blowing over the wall onto his head.|{The library will not reopen until he is found, apparently.|Someone has a sardine. Someone else has a ladder.|A first-year is trying to bribe him with a sock.}}
text [9d326c] = {图书馆的猫脚注坐在庭院墙头，死活不肯下来。底下围了一小群人。|脚注又在庭院墙头上接受朝拜了。|脚注在墙上。人群给你让开一条路，好像你是专家。} {season == "spring": 花瓣越过墙头落在他头上。|{据说找不到他，图书馆就不开门。|有人拿着沙丁鱼，有人拿着梯子。|一个一年级生想用一只袜子贿赂他。}}
# en: A grey library cat sitting on top of a high courtyard wall, a small crowd of students below calling up to it, one holding out a sardine.
scene [8dbc15] = 一只灰色的图书馆猫坐在高高的庭院墙头，底下一小群学生仰头喊它，其中一人举着一条沙丁鱼。
# en: Climb up after him
opt.left.label [7a4523] = 爬上去抓他
# en: {You climb the ivy, take the cat and come down to applause. Footnote looks as if he arranged the whole thing.|You get him on the second try. He purrs, for the crowd only.|You're up the wall before the crowd can offer the ladder. Footnote walks into your arms as if he's been waiting all afternoon.}
opt.left.say.1 [37d75a] = {你顺着常春藤爬上去，抱下猫，赢得一片掌声。脚注一副这一切都是他安排的样子。|你第二次才抓住他。他呼噜呼噜的，只是演给观众看。|人群还没递来梯子，你已经上了墙。脚注走进你怀里，好像等了一下午。}
# en: {The ivy gives. You land in the flowerbed. Footnote walks down the ladder someone else brought.|You get halfway, and Footnote jumps down past you and walks off. The crowd's sympathy is mostly laughter.|You slip at the top. He watches you fall with professional interest, then comes down by himself.}
opt.left.say.2 [b40ff8] = {常春藤断了。你掉进了花坛。脚注顺着别人搬来的梯子走了下来。|你爬到一半，脚注从你身边跳下去走掉了。人群的同情大多是笑声。|你在墙顶滑了一下。他以专业的兴趣看着你掉下去，然后自己下来了。}
# en: Wait him out with the crowd
opt.right.label [6505d4] = 和人群一起等他下来
# en: {You stand with the crowd and trade news while Footnote ignores you all. He comes down when he's bored, which takes an hour.|You chat with the others until the cat gives up. Someone shares a pastry. Footnote takes half.|You spend the hour in good company under the wall. Footnote comes down and sits on your foot, to make a point.}
opt.right.say.1 [56d83c] = {你和人群站在一起交换消息，脚注对你们一概不理。他无聊了才下来，花了一个小时。|你和其他人聊天，直到猫放弃。有人分了块点心。脚注拿走了一半。|你在墙下和大家度过了愉快的一小时。脚注下来后坐在你脚上，以示态度。}

@event company_card_widow
# en: The Widow's Game
title [14d27e] = 寡妇的牌局
# en: {Tonight's guest is a widow in black lace who has come up from the river towns to play cards with somebody young. She deals before you've sat down.|The widow is back, and asked for you by description: "the one who loses nicely."|The widow again. She has brought her own deck this time, and a flask she says is cough syrup.} The landlady murmurs: she tips the ones who make her laugh, and she always knows who's letting her win.
text [39db69] = {今晚的客人是一位穿黑色蕾丝的寡妇，她从河边的镇子上来，想找个年轻人打牌。你还没坐下，她就发好了牌。|那位寡妇又来了，点名要你，原话是：“输得很体面的那个。”|又是那位寡妇。这次她带了自己的牌，还有一个小酒壶，她说里面是止咳糖浆。} 老板娘低声说：能逗她笑的人她就给小费，而且谁在让她赢，她总是一清二楚。
# en: A tavern's upstairs room after midnight, an elegant old woman in black dealing cards at a small table, a student in a borrowed jacket sitting opposite her.
scene [ce383a] = 午夜后酒馆楼上的房间，一位优雅的黑衣老妇人在小桌边发牌，一名穿着借来外套的学生坐在她对面。
# en: Play her honestly, and well
opt.left.label [82766b] = 老老实实，好好打
# en: She tips for a good game; she may take your purse instead.
opt.left.hint [9ef871] = 打得好她会给小费；也可能把你的钱包赢走。
# en: {You play your best and lose by a hair, and she laughs until she has to take her spectacles off. She tips you twice what you'd have won.|You beat her, once, and she's so pleased she tells you about her late husband's three duels. You go home at four, paid and full of stories.|You keep it close all night. When she leaves she pinches your cheek, presses a fold of notes on you, and says, "Next time, cheat a little. It's more fun."}
opt.left.say.1 [104b7c] = {你使出全力，以毫厘之差输了，她笑得不得不摘下眼镜。给你的小费是你本该赢的两倍。|你赢了她一次，她高兴得给你讲了她亡夫的三场决斗。你凌晨四点才回去，钱包满了，故事也满了。|你整晚都咬得很紧。她走时捏了捏你的脸，塞给你一卷钞票，说：“下次稍微作点弊，更好玩。”}
# en: {She sees through you in three hands, and is bored by the fourth. A small tip and an early night.|She plays you off the table, kindly, and tips like a woman who has won. It is not much.|You try too hard to amuse her. She pats your hand. "Never mind, dear," she says, and leaves early.}
opt.left.say.2 [4a9f2c] = {三手牌她就看穿了你，第四手就没了兴致。一点小费，早早收工。|她和蔼地把你打下了牌桌，小费给得像个赢家。没多少。|你太想逗她开心了。她拍拍你的手。“没关系，亲爱的。”她说完就早早走了。}
# en: Let her win, gracefully
opt.right.label [4b092b] = 体面地让她赢
# en: Steady pay, and you know what she thinks of it.
opt.right.hint [3ce8f3] = 报酬稳定，而你知道她怎么看。
# en: {You lose with care all night. She knows, and tips you anyway, the way you'd tip a waiter for a bad soup.|You let her win. She thanks you very politely, which stings more than you expected.|You lose gracefully, as the landlady asked. The widow gives you exactly the going rate, and not a coin more.}
opt.right.say.1 [68e88b] = {你整晚小心翼翼地输。她心知肚明，还是给了小费，就像给端来一碗难喝汤的侍者小费。|你让她赢了。她非常客气地向你道谢，这比你想的更刺人。|你按老板娘的吩咐体面地输了。寡妇给了你不多不少的行价。}
